      "content": "<p>The correct order of increasing intermolecular hydrogen bond strength is :</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "HCN < H<sub>2</sub>O < NH<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "HCN < CH<sub>4</sub> < NH<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "CH<sub>4</sub> < HCN < NH<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "CH<sub>4</sub> < NH<sub>3</sub> < HCN"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "C"
      ],
      "explanation": "Due to the high difference in electronegativity of H and\nN the H-bond strength of NH<sub>3</sub> is highest. There is\nno H-bond in CH<sub>4</sub>.<br/><br/>\nCH<sub>4</sub> < HCN < NH<sub>3</sub>"
